  "body": "This PR depends on #3387 and #3353. Both are merged. The GitHub base is `main`. Commit `3572ca334` contains only the Slot change.\n\nThe Slot Passes tab shows a disabled Auto row and explains why a radial order has no meaning here. A tool-width groove has one centreline. A wider groove connects neighbouring rows and finishes along its wall. Each connected pass must keep its cutting sequence. The MCP add and edit paths now explain this when a caller supplies `pass_start`. No Slot field is stored. The planner keeps its original output.\n\n**Hand trace.** For a 10 mm groove, a 4 mm cutter, a 0.5 mm allowance at each wall, and a 2 mm stepover, the offsets are -2.5, -0.5, +1.5, and +2.5 mm. The tool traverses consecutive rows in opposite directions. Each link joins adjacent ends. The wall lap starts at the end of the last row.\n\n## Refresh on main\n\nThe branch now has a merge of `origin/main` at `bd2b774a8`. The merge class is DELTA: one conflict was resolved by hand.\n\n- Conflict file: `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/pass_start.rs`.\n- Both sides added tests at the same place. The resolution keeps the Slot test, main's newer Adaptive2D test, and main's pass-start status-line test.\n- The resolution drops the obsolete \"Adaptive2D has no pass-start row yet\" test. Main's #3355 made that assertion false.\n- The conflict held no Slot logic and no safety rule.\n\n## Readings on the refreshed head\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 32 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. Wall time 6.5 min, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3`, no sccache.\n- `slot_refuses_a_pass_start_with_its_reason_without_editing_the_job` (`camcraft-app`, `mcp`): pass. It covers add and edit for the values inside, outside, auto, and null. It proves that no rejected patch enters the history.\n- `the_slot_passes_tab_locks_auto_and_names_the_continuous_pass` (`camcraft-ui`, lib): pass. It checks the disabled Auto row and the visible reason.\n- `cargo clippy -j 3 -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: pass.\n\nheavy not run - owed to the cut\n\n## Screenshots\n\n**Face Passes before** (`59b42c727`)\n\n![Face Passes before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/a86a985867ce58c08506006b336c163fc81e0419/3401/3401-stack-face-before.png)\n\n**Face Passes after** (`3572ca334`)\n\n![Face Passes after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/a86a985867ce58c08506006b336c163fc81e0419/3401/3401-stack-face-after.png)\n\n**Slot Passes before** (`59b42c727`)\n\n![Slot Passes before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/a86a985867ce58c08506006b336c163fc81e0419/3401/3401-stack-slot-before.png)\n\n**Slot Passes after** (`3572ca334`)\n\n![Slot Passes after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/a86a985867ce58c08506006b336c163fc81e0419/3401/3401-slot-after.png)\n\n## Verification on the original head `3572ca334`\n\n- `slot_refuses_a_pass_start_with_its_reason_without_editing_the_job` failed on the parent with a generic unknown-field reply. On this head it passes for add and edit, including inside, outside, auto, and null.\n- `the_slot_passes_tab_locks_auto_and_names_the_continuous_pass` first failed because the row was missing. It passes on this head.\n- The nine Slot motion checks, the swept-area check and both committed Slot CL files pass. The centreline and the wider serpentine keep their output.\n- All 31 planned quick steps passed on `3572ca334`. The full UI library suite needed local loopback and Metal access. Its rerun passed 1,426 tests with seven ignored.\n\nClippy passed for all targets in the app and UI crates with warnings denied. The quick plan ran 426 app tests and 1,464 UI tests. Against the immediate parent `6e2d7d8f0`, all 204 selected release-mode execution steps passed the gate. They ran 46 passing tests and reproduced the two registered expected failures (#1950 and #2849). The 17 batches compiled each selected suite on demand. The separate compile-only pass for all app test binaries was omitted to fit the available disk space. No machine run was needed for this UI and diagnostic change.\n\nChangelog: Slot explains its fixed pass order in the Passes tab and through MCP.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3357\n",
